rue,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"910b9d4dd5651d45c170389b8f59983d","RawContent":"[quote name=\"jessiker05\" post=\"1896562\" timestamp=\"1431998498\"]\n\n\nIt isn&#039;t a restaurant but it&#039;s a little spot kind of on the side of the main pool (I think).. here are some pics..[\/quote]\n@[member=\"jessiker05\"] I know exactly where this is. It is adjacent to the main pool. You can see part of the pool on the other side of the columns. I believe the windows opposite the columns are a restaurant. It&#039;s pretty spot and it looks great in the pix with the receptions set up.","Attachments":[],"Id":1896568,"PostDate":1432011400,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>jessiker05, on 18 May 2015 - 06:21 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>It isn't a restaurant but it's a little spot kind of on the side of the main pool (I think).. here are some pics..<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"279800\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/279800-jessiker05\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">jessiker05<\/span><\/a> I know exactly where this is. It is adjacent to the main pool. You can see part of the pool on the other side of the columns. I believe the windows opposite the columns are a restaurant. It's pretty spot and it looks great in the pix with the receptions set up.\u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>- Erin<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My planning thread:\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79068-vancouverpetunia-now-sapphire-april-7-2016\/?p=1893268'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79068-vancouverpetunia-now-sapphire-april-7-2016\/?p=1893268<\/a>","Email":"ekjzwedding@gmail.com","IpAddress":"24.85.127.174","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1417453045,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281283.jpg?_r=1428779369","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"vancouverpetunia","Id":281283,"Name":"vancouverpetunia","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"24.222.45.206","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"235b4fde6d54d9d15cd4e00b96e8cb2f","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"vancouverpetunia\"] yeah, I don&#039;t think I&#039;d want to have a dinner there, but cocktail hour should be fine, I hope! Might be a little awkward depending on how well my guests and the pool-goers can see each other lol..&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1896570,"PostDate":1432041380,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"281283\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281283-vancouverpetunia\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">vancouverpetunia<\/span><\/a> yeah, I don't think I'd want to have a dinner there, but cocktail hour should be fine, I hope! Might be a little awkward depending on how well my guests and the pool-goers can see each other lol..<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p><span style=\"color:#800080;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><em><span style=\"font-family:'times new roman', times, serif;\">Jessica<\/span><\/em><\/span><\/strong><\/span>","Email":"jessiker05@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"24.222.45.206","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1410546713,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-279800.jpg?_r=1432039880","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":164,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"jessiker05","Id":279800,"Name":"jessiker05","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.72.41.59","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"7a0d0a44b270f4728bac97c4faeb1a95","RawContent":"[quote name=\"JaxBchKay\" post=\"1896561\" timestamp=\"1431995832\"]\nThank you!  We danced down the aisle to Bruno Mars \"Marry You\" and then back up the aisle to \"Happy\" :)  We wanted to just enjoy every minute and we did! \n\nI have to say, I love how colorful your wedding was!  I bet your hubby was very happy he got to wear shorts, mine wanted to but I wouldn&#039;t let him :)[\/quote]I&#039;m glad you did :)  like I said I was sooo nervous but by the time we had the reception I was ready to let loose. Can&#039;t wait to see your video :)\n\nThanks!! I didn&#039;t have a theme just wanted bright colors. Thankfully it all worked out.  Haha shorts were always a must have. They would have died otherwise.  Even the BMs in their dresses were soaking wet. It was a hot day! \n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1896571,"PostDate":1432044309,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>JaxBchKay, on 18 May 2015 - 05:37 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'><p>Thank you!  We danced down the aisle to Bruno Mars \"Marry You\" and then back up the aisle to \"Happy\" <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>  We wanted to just enjoy every minute and we did! <br><br>\nI have to say, I love how colorful your wedding was!  I bet your hubby was very happy he got to wear shorts, mine wanted to but I wouldn't let him <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p><\/div><\/div>\n<br>\nI'm glad you did <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>  like I said I was sooo nervous but by the time we had the reception I was ready to let loose. Can't wait to see your video <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><br><br>\nThanks!! I didn't have a theme just wanted bright colors. Thankfully it all worked out.  Haha shorts were always a must have. They would have died otherwise.  Even the BMs in their dresses were soaking wet. It was a hot day! <br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>Married on 2015\/01\/21 at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya with 43 guests in attendance \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Review\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399432202,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"198.137.185.16","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"b0f70d5cf27f8019f757d5c69e39ee64","RawContent":"[quote name=\"jessiker05\" post=\"1896570\" timestamp=\"1432037780\"]\n@[member=\"vancouverpetunia\"] yeah, I don&#039;t think I&#039;d want to have a dinner there, but cocktail hour should be fine, I hope! Might be a little awkward depending on how well my guests and the pool-goers can see each other lol..[\/quote]\nThat part of pool was almost always empty while we were there - everyone is around the bar and gazebo at the other end so you are fine on that.  The only thing that might be a little annoying is on the beach side of that terrace is the hostess station for the BlueWater Grille and there is a bar there also for people waiting to be seated.  If your wedding is on a night that the BlueWater is closed, it won&#039;t be a problem but if it&#039;s open, then people will be around and your view of the beach\/water might be a bit blocked.  Since it&#039;s only for cocktail hour and people are walking around anyway I&#039;m sure it will be fine, and the will sort of block it off so people won&#039;t be walking through or anything. \n\n@[member=\"calgarybride2015\"] - It was hot, and my hubby&#039;s shirt was completely soaked by the end of the night, but we snuck down to the beach a couple of times where we had a great breeze and cooled off.  Your bright colors worked out beautifully!!\n[quote name=\"jessiker05\" post=\"1896562\" timestamp=\"1431998498\"]\n@[member=\"JaxBchKay\"] Awesome pictures! Looks like it was a perfect day! You looked gorgeous - I love your dress! I&#039;m also using turquoise as my colors.. I love how your table was setup, did you bring all the little candles? Thanks for sharing! \n\n\nIt isn&#039;t a restaurant but it&#039;s a little spot kind of on the side of the main pool (I think).. here are some pics..[\/quote]Thank you so much!  I had the second dress just for dinner and dancing which was nice and I twisted my hair into a bun so it was cooler :) \n\nI brought a ton of the decor with me, the little blue candle holders, the shell candle holders, the table runners, chair sashes, the candles, a few vases, etc. etc.  So I have 3 dozen turquoise candle holders and battery operated candles.  I&#039;m willing to sell some of them if you are interested, along with chair sashes and table runners :)","Attachments":[],"Id":1896572,"PostDate":1432045752,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>jessiker05, on 19 May 2015 - 05:16 AM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"281283\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281283-vancouverpetunia\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">vancouverpetunia<\/span><\/a> yeah, I don't think I'd want to have a dinner there, but cocktail hour should be fine, I hope! Might be a little awkward depending on how well my guests and the pool-goers can see each other lol..<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>That part of pool was almost always empty while we were there - everyone is around the bar and gazebo at the other end so you are fine on that.\u00a0 The only thing that might be a little annoying is on the beach side of that terrace is the hostess station for the BlueWater Grille and there is a bar there also for people waiting to be seated.\u00a0 If your wedding is on a night that the BlueWater is closed, it won't be a problem but if it's open, then people will be around and your view of the beach\/water might be a bit blocked.\u00a0 Since it's only for cocktail hour and people are walking around anyway I'm sure it will be fine, and the will sort of block it off so people won't be walking through or anything.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"277873\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/277873-calgarybride2015\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">calgarybride2015<\/span><\/a> - It was hot, and my hubby's shirt was completely soaked by the end of the night, but we snuck down to the beach a couple of times where we had a great breeze and cooled off.\u00a0 Your bright colors worked out beautifully!!<\/p><br \/><p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>jessiker05, on 18 May 2015 - 06:21 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"267461\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/267461-jaxbchkay\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">JaxBchKay<\/span><\/a> Awesome pictures! Looks like it was a perfect day! You looked gorgeous - I love your dress! I'm also using turquoise as my colors.. I love how your table was setup, did you bring all the little candles? Thanks for sharing!\u00a0<\/p>\n<br><p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>It isn't a restaurant but it's a little spot kind of on the side of the main pool (I think).. here are some pics..<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>Thank you so much!\u00a0 I had the second dress just for dinner and dancing which was nice and I twisted my hair into a bun so it was cooler <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I brought a ton of the decor with me, the little blue candle holders, the shell candle holders, the table runners, chair sashes, the candles, a few vases, etc. etc.\u00a0 So I have 3 dozen turquoise candle holders and battery operated candles.\u00a0 I'm willing to sell some of them if you are interested, along with chair sashes and table runners <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>\u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"karinbean@pgatourhq.com","IpAddress":"67.190.225.116","GroupId":47,"GroupName":"Site Supporter","JoinDate":1363562092,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-267461.jpg?_r=1430657102","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"JaxBchKay","Id":267461,"Name":"JaxBchKay","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"24.222.45.206","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"40144a8c6c7e5a7210ed651d672a8d9f","RawContent":"[quote name=\"JaxBchKay\" post=\"1896572\" timestamp=\"1432042152\"]\nThank you so much!  I had the second dress just for dinner and dancing which was nice and I twisted my hair into a bun so it was cooler :)\n\nI brought a ton of the decor with me, the little blue candle holders, the shell candle holders, the table runners, chair sashes, the candles, a few vases, etc. etc.  So I have 3 dozen turquoise candle holders and battery operated candles.  I&#039;m willing to sell some of them if you are interested, along with chair sashes and table runners :)[\/quote]\nHmm, I see you&#039;re located in Florida.. I&#039;m in Nova Scotia - might end up costing me more by the time I ship everything! Plus, I do feel, however, that your colors are a bit on the blue side, where mine are a bit more on the green side of turquoise! Thanks for the offer though! :)","Attachments":[],"Id":1896581,"PostDate":1432050153,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>JaxBchKay, on 19 May 2015 - 06:29 AM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>Thank you so much!\u00a0 I had the second dress just for dinner and dancing which was nice and I twisted my hair into a bun so it was cooler <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I brought a ton of the decor with me, the little blue candle holders, the shell candle holders, the table runners, chair sashes, the candles, a few vases, etc. etc.\u00a0 So I have 3 dozen turquoise candle holders and battery operated candles.\u00a0 I'm willing to sell some of them if you are interested, along with chair sashes and table runners <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Hmm, I see you're located in Florida.. I'm in Nova Scotia - might end up costing me more by the time I ship everything! Plus, I do feel, however, that your colors are a bit on the blue side, where mine are a bit more on the green side of turquoise! Thanks for the offer though! <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p><span style=\"color:#800080;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><em><span style=\"font-family:'times new roman', times, serif;\">Jessica<\/span><\/em><\/span><\/strong><\/span>","Email":"jessiker05@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"24.222.45.206","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1410546713,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-279800.jpg?_r=1432039880","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":164,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"jessiker05","Id":279800,"Name":"jessiker05","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"47.21.46.58","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"9c917a4d95c2c765dff153f655553a3d","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"Ashleyg280\"]&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;My fiance is an attorney. If you have it in writing that you&#039;ve got that space, then that&#039;s a contract. She broke it. They need to do WAAAAAAY more than just give you some sort of compensation - which I assume wouldn&#039;t be anything significant. Honestly, you could probably take her to small claims court and sue. I&#039;m not a very drastic person but when it comes to something like your wedding, it&#039;s something worth considering.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Have you been in touch with anyone at the resort? You should&#039;ve been introduced to your wedding coordinator. You should&#039;ve also gotten a more detailed contract directly from the resort.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1896584,"PostDate":1432050857,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"282903\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/282903-ashleyg280\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">Ashleyg280<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My fiance is an attorney. If you have it in writing that you've got that space, then that's a contract. She broke it. They need to do WAAAAAAY more than just give you some sort of compensation - which I assume wouldn't be anything significant. Honestly, you could probably take her to small claims court and sue. I'm not a very drastic person but when it comes to something like your wedding, it's something worth considering.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Have you been in touch with anyone at the resort? You should've been introduced to your wedding coordinator. You should've also gotten a more detailed contract directly from the resort.\u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"robynbrooke81@gmail.com","IpAddress":"75.99.18.219","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1403550989,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-278661.jpg?_r=1404161707","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":267,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"jeffandrobyn","Id":278661,"Name":"jeffandrobyn","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"99.247.97.154","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"<strong>Edited by cvooys, 19 May 2015 - 11:02 AM.<\/strong>","EditDate":1432062160,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"f5eaf6ba406f35f766bef0ba76feb5f0","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;I&#039;m getting married at the Now Sapphire on September 14 and I&#039;m curious about how other brides did their bachelorette parties?&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I&#039;m a little bit nervous about having all my girls leaving the resort and getting drunk. Did any of you stay on the resort for your bachelorette?&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I&#039;m open to suggestions! Thanks!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1896602,"PostDate":1432062145,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>I'm getting married at the Now Sapphire on September 14 and I'm curious about how other brides did their bachelorette parties?<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I'm a little bit nervous about having all my girls leaving the resort and getting drunk. Did any of you stay on the resort for your bachelorette?<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I'm open to suggestions! Thanks!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"colleen.vooys@yahoo.ca","IpAddress":"70.50.13.225","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1431538083,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"cvooys","Id":283085,"Name":"cvooys","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"24.22.51.186","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"adebf254d80d3dbb9c10070673f008b7","RawContent":"[quote name=\"jeffandrobyn\" post=\"1896584\" timestamp=\"1432047257\"]\n@[member=\"Ashleyg280\"]\n\nMy fiance is an attorney. If you have it in writing that you&#039;ve got that space, then that&#039;s a contract. She broke it. They need to do WAAAAAAY more than just give you some sort of compensation - which I assume wouldn&#039;t be anything significant. Honestly, you could probably take her to small claims court and sue. I&#039;m not a very drastic person but when it comes to something like your wedding, it&#039;s something worth considering. \n\nHave you been in touch with anyone at the resort? You should&#039;ve been introduced to your wedding coordinator. You should&#039;ve also gotten a more detailed contract directly from the resort.[\/quote]\n@[member=\"jeffandrobyn\"] Destinantionwedding.com got back to us today saying they would give us $150 credit towards our room contract. They are saying that the original form I sent them with my request of time, locations and date they were not able to open. Going back it does look like it was done on my mac using a program called pages, so if she didn&#039;t have an apple computer or phone it wouldn&#039;t have opened. Regardless what would make her think that she should just go ahead and make the decision on when and where I would want to have my wedding! And then a week later when I asked her point blank, did I get the time, date, and locations I requested would she say absolutely.  At that moment she should have said she never opened the form and didn&#039;t know what I requested.  Ahhh it is SOO frustrating dealing with them. I really wanted to believe that she would finally apologize for her mistake and make it right. I feel like a wedding travel agency site like destination wedding.com don&#039;t even care about their customer services because most likely the people they screw over will never be getting married again, and have no use for them again.","Attachments":[],"Id":1896624,"PostDate":1432091356,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>jeffandrobyn, on 19 May 2015 - 07:54 AM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"282903\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/282903-ashleyg280\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">Ashleyg280<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My fiance is an attorney. If you have it in writing that you've got that space, then that's a contract. She broke it. They need to do WAAAAAAY more than just give you some sort of compensation - which I assume wouldn't be anything significant. Honestly, you could probably take her to small claims court and sue. I'm not a very drastic person but when it comes to something like your wedding, it's something worth considering.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Have you been in touch with anyone at the resort? You should've been introduced to your wedding coordinator. You should've also gotten a more detailed contract directly from the resort.\u00a0<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"278661\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/278661-jeffandrobyn\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">jeffandrobyn<\/span><\/a> Destinantionwedding.com got back to us today saying they would give us $150 credit towards our room contract. They are saying that the original form I sent them with my request of time, locations and date they were not able to open. Going back it does look like it was done on my mac using a program called pages, so if she didn't have an apple computer or phone it wouldn't have opened. Regardless what would make her think that she should just go ahead and make the decision on when and where I would want to have my wedding! And then a week later when I asked her point blank, did I get the time, date, and locations I requested would she say absolutely. \u00a0At that moment she should have said she never opened the form and didn't know what I requested. \u00a0Ahhh it is SOO frustrating dealing with them. I really wanted to believe that she would finally apologize for her mistake and make it right. I feel like a wedding travel agency site like destination wedding.com don't even care about their customer services because most likely the people they screw over will never be getting married again, and have no use for them again.<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"ashleyg280@gmail.com","IpAddress":"24.22.51.186","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1430274601,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-282903.jpg?_r=1436298269","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"facebook"},"FormattedName":"Ashleyg280","Id":282903,"Name":"Ashleyg280","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"24.85.127.174","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"d462f38a3b444f262739aae8034ec6df","RawContent":"[quote name=\"cvooys\" post=\"1896602\" timestamp=\"1432058545\"]\nI&#039;m getting married at the Now Sapphire on September 14 and I&#039;m curious about how other brides did their bachelorette parties?\n\nI&#039;m a little bit nervous about having all my girls leaving the resort and getting drunk. Did any of you stay on the resort for your bachelorette?\n\nI&#039;m open to suggestions! Thanks![\/quote]\n@[member=\"cvooys\"] - I will likely do something at home, a few weeks before we leave. We&#039;ll already have 2 pretty full days with our guests (wedding and excursion), and I figure they may want some time on their own as well, so I don&#039;t want to plan too many events. Plus we may have some people who can&#039;t come to Mexico but would like to come to the bachelorette party.","Attachments":[],"Id":1896632,"PostDate":1432102581,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>cvooys, on 19 May 2015 - 11:02 AM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>I'm getting married at the Now Sapphire on September 14 and I'm curious about how other brides did their bachelorette parties?<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I'm a little bit nervous about having all my girls leaving the resort and getting drunk. Did any of you stay on the resort for your bachelorette?<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I'm open to suggestions! Thanks!<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"283085\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/283085-cvooys\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">cvooys<\/span><\/a> - I will likely do something at home, a few weeks before we leave. We'll already have 2 pretty full days with our guests (wedding and excursion), and I figure they may want some time on their own as well, so I don't want to plan too many events. Plus we may have some people who can't come to Mexico but would like to come to the bachelorette party.<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>- Erin<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My planning thread:\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79068-vancouverpetunia-now-sapphire-april-7-2016\/?p=1893268'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79068-vancouverpetunia-now-sapphire-april-7-2016\/?p=1893268<\/a>","Email":"ekjzwedding@gmail.com","IpAddress":"24.85.127.174","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1417453045,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281283.jpg?_r=1428779369","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"vancouverpetunia","Id":281283,"Name":"vancouverpetunia","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"198.137.185.16","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"fe9ccd4a2b61ff5791f7cbae5e63990f","RawContent":"[quote name=\"cvooys\" post=\"1896602\" timestamp=\"1432058545\"]\nI&#039;m getting married at the Now Sapphire on September 14 and I&#039;m curious about how other brides did their bachelorette parties?\n\nI&#039;m a little bit nervous about having all my girls leaving the resort and getting drunk. Did any of you stay on the resort for your bachelorette?\n\nI&#039;m open to suggestions! Thanks![\/quote]I had my bachelorette party at home about a month before we left for Mexico.  That way I got to include ladies that weren&#039;t able to come on the trip.  It was also better because we didn&#039;t have to worry about leaving the resort and spending money in another country.  My hubby and his best man did go into Cancun one evening and he said that he wouldn&#039;t not have wanted me to go with my girls alone.","Attachments":[],"Id":1896638,"PostDate":1432125429,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>cvooys, on 19 May 2015 - 11:02 AM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>I'm getting married at the Now Sapphire on September 14 and I'm curious about how other brides did their bachelorette parties?<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I'm a little bit nervous about having all my girls leaving the resort and getting drunk. Did any of you stay on the resort for your bachelorette?<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I'm open to suggestions! Thanks!<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>I had my bachelorette party at home about a month before we left for Mexico.\u00a0 That way I got to include ladies that weren't able to come on the trip.\u00a0 It was also better because we didn't have to worry about leaving the resort and spending money in another country.\u00a0 My hubby and his best man did go into Cancun one evening and he said that he wouldn't not have wanted me to go with my girls alone.\u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"karinbean@pgatourhq.com","IpAddress":"67.190.225.116","GroupId":47,"GroupName":"Site Supporter","JoinDate":1363562092,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-267461.jpg?_r=1430657102","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"JaxBchKay","Id":267461,"Name":"JaxBchKay","IsOnline":false}}],"Id":"62152","Title":"Now Sapphire Weddings Formerly Paradisus Riviera","LastPostDate":1440426594},"Pages":{"TotalItems":2693,"TotalPages":270,"CurrentPage":2590,"NextPage":2600,"PreviousPage":2580,"LastPage":2690},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":1,"Type":"int"}]}
